# C-to-Rust port (copy into the target repo)

Architectural invariants for a C library port. Enable `alwaysApply` only while the port is in progress. Do not keep this always-on after the port ships.

Full playbook: `.cursor/skills/port-c-library-to-rust/SKILL.md`.

## MUST

- Cargo workspace: `{lib}-core` holds all logic with `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`. `{lib}-ffi` is a thin C ABI shim (`#[repr(C)]`, original header symbols, `staticlib` + `cdylib`).
- `{lib}-ffi` is the **only** crate that may contain `unsafe`. Every `unsafe` block has a `SAFETY:` comment.
- Keep original `*.c` / `*.h` in-tree as the behavioral spec and oracle. Do not delete them once Rust compiles.
- Match C **including quirks**. Do not "fix" lookup case folding, duplicate keys, print formatting, NaN/Inf, nesting limits, or error offsets.
- Malformed input returns `Result` / `Error`. Library code must not panic on untrusted data.
- Port the original test suite (Unity or equivalent). Same cases, not a replacement suite.
- Differential harness vs original C: parse success/failure, exact error position on failure, byte-identical compact **and** pretty print. Exit nonzero on divergence.
- `PARITY.md`: per-input table, documented quirks with **C source lines**, divergences or "none".
- `MIGRATION.md`: layout, `grep -rn "unsafe" --include=*.rs` (exclude `target/`), kept quirks vs intentional diffs.
- Name out-of-scope APIs explicitly (silent skip is a bug).
- `cargo test` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` must pass.

## MUST NOT

- Put parse/print/tree logic in the FFI crate.
- Compare only "parses or not" or pretty JSON that is merely close.
- Treat a green test run as proof without `PARITY.md`.
- Invent a new public API that existing C callers cannot use through the original header.
